description:
FILED s526w1 (Opus, 2026-10-24) from the URI-5.34 board census.  PRE-EXISTING (main 761d92f4 gives the same).

A class whose name has TWO OR MORE all-capital segments (URI::URL, URI::IRI, UU::RL) does not find an INHERITED AUTOLOAD and does not find an inherited `""` OVERLOAD.  Ordinary inherited methods (new) are found, `->can` works; a single-segment all-caps name (UURL) and a mixed-case name (Url) work.  The :invert reader case flip of an all-caps segment is the first suspect (the AUTOLOAD / overload lookups resolve the class by a different spelling than method dispatch does) -- the cheap discriminator: print the CL package / class name each lookup builds for "UU::RL".

REPRO (scratch/s526w1/pr/autoload2.pl):
    package Inner; sub new { bless {}, shift } sub scheme { "http" } sub as_string { "STR" }
    package Wb; use overload '""' => "as_string", fallback => 1; sub as_string;
    sub new { bless [Inner->new], shift }
    our $AUTOLOAD; sub AUTOLOAD { my $s = shift; my $m = substr($AUTOLOAD, rindex($AUTOLOAD, '::') + 2);
      return if $m eq "DESTROY"; $s->[0]->$m(@_) }
    package UU::RL; our @ISA = ('Wb');
    package main; my $u = UU::RL->new; print $u->scheme, " [$u]\n";
  perl 5.40.3: http [STR]
  PCL: dies  Can't locate object method "scheme" via package "UU::RL"
  (without the ->scheme call: perl [STR], PCL [UU::RL=ARRAY(0x1)] -- the overload is missed too)

Consumers on the board (URI): mix.t (whole file, 6 rows), old-base.t (stops at row 1 of ~30), old-relbase.t rows 4-5, heuristic.t (stops at row 18 of 28), iri.t (stops at row 14 of 30: URI::IRI->as_iri).  URI::URL is LWP's legacy interface, so this reaches every old LWP user.
